---
/*
 * Section 8 — for your clients, not just your practice.
 *
 * This is the section that changes what the page is worth to a firm. Everything before
 * it offers to take work off the practice; this offers to fix the thing upstream that
 * creates the work in the first place. It is also the one section where a reader could
 * suspect a conflict of interest, which is why the third beat exists and why it gets its
 * own panel rather than being buried at the end of a paragraph. A CPA reading "no
 * referral fee and no margin" needs to find it without hunting.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The /workshop link is mine, not the doc's.
 *
 * The doc's internal-links list requires a link to /workshop from sections 8 and 9.
 * Section 9 has a natural anchor — step 2 is literally called "The workshop". Section 8
 * does not: its copy never mentions the workshop, so there was no phrase to attach a
 * link to and Fredrick asked me to build one.
 *
 * It is a standalone link rather than added prose, and its label is exactly "The
 * workshop" — the same label the site footer already uses for that destination, so the
 * two agree. It makes no claim and adds no sentence to copy that was argued over. If it
 * should say something else, it is one string.
 *
 * NOTE: /workshop does not exist yet and currently 404s. Both links on this page point
 * at it because the doc requires them to. This is the same known gap as the footer's
 * existing "The workshop" link, and it is a launch blocker for the page, not a defect in
 * it. See CLAUDE.md, "Still to build for release one".
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */
---

<section class="clients">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="clients__head">
      <h2 class="clients__title">
        The same system, pointed at the client who keeps sending you a shoebox.
      </h2>
      <p class="clients__body">
        Most of what slows a practice down does not start inside the practice. It starts
        with a client who sends receipts in five formats, three weeks late, and always
        just before a deadline.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="clients__row">
      <div class="clients__main">
        <p class="clients__sub">
          We can build the capture side into that client's own systems rather than yours,
          so what reaches you is already clean and coded and ready for review. You
          introduce us, we work with them directly, and you go back to being their
          accountant.
        </p>

        <a class="clients__workshop" href="/workshop">
          The workshop
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4.5 12h14M13 6.5 18.5 12 13 17.5" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      {/* The conflict-of-interest answer. Given its own block so it is findable. */}
      <div class="clients__panel">
        <span class="clients__panel-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 3.4 4.9 6.4v5c0 4.2 2.9 8 7.1 9.2 4.2-1.2 7.1-5 7.1-9.2v-5z" />
            <path d="m9.2 11.9 2.3 2.3 4.2-4.5" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <p>
          There is no referral fee and no margin, which means there is nothing for you to
          disclose and nothing that could look like an interest in the recommendation.
          What you get is a client whose records arrive on time and in one piece. We do
          not sell them anything else, and we do not go around you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .clients {
    background: var(--ark-cream);
    padding-block: 96px;
  }

  .clients__title {
    font-size: var(--ark-h2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  .clients__body {
    margin-top: 26px;
    max-width: 66ch;
    font-size: 1.16rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #5b564e;
  }

  .clients__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 44px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 44px;
  }

  .clients__sub {
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #5b564e;
  }

  .clients__workshop {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ark-olive);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--ark-olive-2);
  }

  .clients__workshop:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--ark-olive);
  }

  .clients__workshop svg {
    width: 17px;
    height: 17px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .clients__panel {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 18px;
    background: var(--ark-green-soft);
    border-radius: var(--ark-radius);
    padding: 30px 32px;
  }

  .clients__panel-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ark-olive);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .clients__panel-icon svg {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
  }

  .clients__panel p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.66;
    color: var(--ark-charcoal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .clients__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .clients {
      padding-block: 56px;
    }

    .clients__body {
      margin-top: 20px;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .clients__row {
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .clients__sub {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .clients__panel {
      padding: 24px 22px;
      gap: 14px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px), (orientation: portrait) {
    .clients__title {
      text-align: center;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
